{
  "description": "The partitions section of the application admin (partitions contract section 11, admin contract section 3a), written by hand for the Go build; the Java framework follows from it. Setup: application 'acme' with the admin skeleton and the partitions section (id 'partitions', path /admin/partitions, permission acme:admin:partitions:view, operators only). 'gate': every operation of the section needs its permission (the GET operations acme:admin:partitions:view, the two POST operations acme:admin:partitions:manage; the wildcard rule of core section 3 applies) AND a caller whose tier is exactly ANCHOR; a PARTNER, a CLIENT and a caller with no tier get 403 FORBIDDEN with a message that says the operation is for platform operators, whatever permissions they hold; a caller without the permission gets 403 FORBIDDEN; 'navigation' says whether GET /api/admin/navigation lists the section for that caller (it also needs acme:admin:console:view, which every case holds). A case's 'view' and 'manage' give whether a caller may use the operations of that permission (true: not refused by the gate; false: 403 FORBIDDEN). 'durations': a declared duration on the wire is ISO-8601 as java.time.Duration.toString writes it. 'projection': a table's status (neutral input: instants RFC 3339, durations in seconds, a null is absent) and the two documents the section writes from it, 'summary' (an item of GET /api/admin/partitions, 'tables') and 'table' (GET /api/admin/partitions/{table}); an absent optional field is omitted, not null; 'summary.partitionCount', 'bytes' and 'rows' are the table's totals, 'oldestFrom' is the first partition's from (partitions are listed oldest first), 'nextRemovalDue' the earliest removalDue of its partitions. 'refusals': requests of an operator holding both permissions against an application whose declared tables are 'readings' (monthly, ahead 2, id-keyed) and 'samples' (weekly), answered with the status and error code given; 'table' in a path is a table as declared or schema-qualified. Documents are compared as parsed JSON.",
  "howToRun": "gate: for every case and every operation, send the request with the case's tier and permissions and compare allowed or refused. durations: format each. projection: map the input to the documents and compare. refusals: send each request as the operator and compare the status and the error code.",
  "application": "acme",
  "operations": [
    {
      "id": "listAdminPartitions",
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/api/admin/partitions",
      "permission": "view"
    },
    {
      "id": "getAdminPartitionTable",
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/api/admin/partitions/{table}",
      "permission": "view"
    },
    {
      "id": "listAdminPartitionArchives",
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/api/admin/partitions/{table}/archives",
      "permission": "view"
    },
    {
      "id": "runAdminPartitionPass",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/admin/partitions/passes",
      "permission": "manage"
    },
    {
      "id": "ensureAdminPartitions",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/admin/partitions/{table}/ensure",
      "permission": "manage"
    }
  ],
